IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Writ Petition (Civil) No. 857 of 2015
CITATION: (2016) 7 SCC 498
YEAR: 2016

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Madan B. Lokur, N.V. Ramana

PARTIES:
Swaraj Abhiyan vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
National Food Security Act, 2013, MGNREGA, 2005, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 21, Article 47

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
drought relief, right to food, distress migration, statutory entitlements

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Issued binding directives for drought management and social security implementation, holding that the right to food is an inseparable entitlement under Article 21.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 21, Article 47.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

